  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4.2.1, 'Roles and contributions of component “building blocks”' to a national eHealth environment. Two groups of building blocks, each block paired with its contributions. ENABLING ENVIRONMENT: leadership, governance and multisector engagement (direct and coordinate eHealth nationally, align with health goals, support change); strategy and investment (a responsive national strategy and plan, with financing aligned to priorities); legislation, policy and compliance (national policies and a legal and enforcement environment that builds trust); workforce (eHealth knowledge and skills, networks, and education and training programmes); and standards and interoperability (consistent, accurate collection and exchange of health information). ICT ENVIRONMENT: infrastructure (networks, core services and applications for information exchange across boundaries) and services and applications (the means of delivering health content and managing information, for the public, patients, providers and others).",
      "state": "draft",
